---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — Pulse Purse"
  description="How Pulse Purse handles your data."
>
  <Header />
  <main class="container legal">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="muted">Last updated: October 2026</p>
    <p>
      Pulse Purse ("we", "us") is a personal finance app operated by Crafton Tech. This policy
      explains what we collect, why, and the choices you have. If anything here is unclear, use
      the <a href="/contact">contact form</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Account details:</strong> your name and email address, and a password (stored only as a one-way hash) if you sign up with email. If you sign in with Google or Apple we receive your name and email from them.</li>
      <li><strong>Phone number:</strong> only if you add one, so we can send payment reminders by SMS.</li>
      <li><strong>Financial records you enter:</strong> income, expenses, budgets, projects, plans and goals, including amounts, dates, categories, currencies and notes.</li>
      <li><strong>Preferences:</strong> for example reminder settings. Your default currency and theme are kept on your device.</li>
      <li><strong>Messages you send us</strong> through the contact form.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do not collect your location, contacts, photos or bank-account credentials, and we do not connect to your bank.</p>

    <h2>How we use it</h2>
    <p>
      To run the app: sign you in, store and show your records, calculate your totals and
      forecasts, and send the reminders you switch on by email or SMS. We do not sell your data and
      we do not use it for advertising or tracking across other companies' apps and websites.
    </p>

    <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
    <p>
      Only service providers that help us run Pulse Purse: our hosting provider, our email and SMS
      delivery providers (they receive your email address or phone number and the reminder text),
      and Google or Apple when you choose to sign in with them. Records you explicitly share
      from a project are visible to the people you share them with. We may disclose data if the law
      requires it.
    </p>

    <h2>Keeping and deleting your data</h2>
    <p>
      We keep your data while your account exists. You can delete your account at any time in the
      app under <em>Profile &rarr; Delete account</em>. This permanently removes your account and
      all of your records from our systems. If you used Sign in with Apple, we also tell Apple to
      revoke the connection. Backups are overwritten on their normal cycle.
    </p>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <p>
      You can view and edit your name, email and phone number in the app, turn reminders off, or
      delete your account. You can also ask us, through the contact form, for a copy of your data
      or a correction.
    </p>

    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>
      Data is sent over encrypted connections and passwords are hashed. No system is perfectly
      secure, so please use a strong, unique password.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>Pulse Purse is not intended for children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect their data.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>If we change this policy in a meaningful way we will update the date above and, where appropriate, tell you in the app.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions or requests: <a href="/contact">pulsepurse.app/contact</a>.</p>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
<style>
  .legal { padding-block: 4rem; max-width: 680px; }
  .legal h1 { margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .legal h2 { margin-top: 2rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; font-size: 1.15rem; }
  .legal p, .legal li { line-height: 1.65; }
  .legal ul { padding-left: 1.25rem; }
</style>
